{"clock":1,"nonce":"ae59e4bd941c831eb8ff2d6dea637568","ops":[{"kind":"create","author":"ee004d31386b76440a74651c79871f156633d4ff","time":1792492663,"origin":{"forge":"github.com/guilbep/git-board","event":"issue:5940201136"},"data":{"body":"Raised while releasing v0.8.0 (2026-10-20). That release was made by hand (tag, `make dist`, `gh release create`), because setting up the Releases page still means editing `.git-board.toml`'s `[release]` table by hand.\n\n**Want:** click and go. The Releases page offers each kind of release with an Enable button, and fills the config itself:\n\n- **Enable web app release**: discovers the images (Dockerfiles), the chart (`helm/`) and the config repo. It infers the registry from the remote in `.git/config`, e.g. `ghcr.io/\u003cowner\u003e/\u003crepo\u003e/\u003cimage\u003e`. The page shows what it found and the user confirms.\n- **Enable binary release**: per-platform archives and checksums attached to the forge's release, what `make dist` + `gh release create` do for git-board itself.\n- **Others**: libraries published to a package registry, and versioned code or scripts, where the tag is the release (see GB-18).\n\n**Done when:** a repo with no `[release]` table gets a working release setup from the Releases page without opening the TOML editor, and git-board's own next release is cut from it.\n\nRelated: GB-18 (kinds of release beyond images and a chart), GB-17 (the pipeline).\n","title":"release: enable it from the Releases page in one click, the config inferred"}},{"kind":"set-status","author":"ee004d31386b76440a74651c79871f156633d4ff","time":1792611698,"origin":{"forge":"github.com/guilbep/git-board","event":"issue:5940201136"},"data":{"status":"closed"}},{"kind":"change-labels","author":"ee004d31386b76440a74651c79871f156633d4ff","time":1792611700,"origin":{"forge":"github.com/guilbep/git-board","event":"issue:5940201136"},"data":{"add":["kind:feat","status:done","assignee:guilbep"],"remove":null}},{"kind":"comment","author":"ee004d31386b76440a74651c79871f156633d4ff","time":1792504204,"origin":{"forge":"github.com/guilbep/git-board","event":"comment:6292426703"},"data":{"body":"Design settled 2026-10-20, with the plan at `~/.claude/plans/gb-19-release-enable-it-goofy-biscuit.md`. **This branch does the binary release only.** Enable web app release, and the others, stay here as later branches.\n\n\nThree keys, no environments:\n\n```toml\n[release]\nbinaries = [\"./cmd/git-board\"]\nplatforms = [\"linux/amd64\", \"linux/arm64\", \"darwin/amd64\", \"darwin/arm64\", \"windows/amd64\"]\nbuild = \"make dist\"   # optional\n```\n\nA table with binaries and no environments is enabled. The existing rules then give what a binary release wants: every cut is a final (no candidate environment), deployed nowhere (no last environment). An artifact kind per entry (GB-18) is deferred: these keys are what a binary entry would say, so they move there later without a rewrite.\n\n\nIn a clean detached checkout of the tag (the `checkout` the deploys use, so `git describe` reports the tag). Built-in: `CGO_ENABLED=0 go build -trimpath -ldflags \"-s -w\"` per platform, a `.tar.gz` (`.zip` for windows) holding `\u003cbinary\u003e_\u003ctag\u003e_\u003cos\u003e_\u003carch\u003e/` with the binary, LICENSE and README.md, and `checksums.txt` (sha256). With `build` set, that command runs instead and whatever it leaves in `dist/` ships: git-board needs this for its embedded web bundle.\n\n\nAfter the tag is pushed: `gh release create \u003ctag\u003e --verify-tag --notes-file …  dist/*`, the notes being the draft's (the issues merged since the previous final), the same as the record's. GitHub only for now, inferred from the remote's URL; a gitlab or gitea remote gets a clear \"not yet\" at Enable time. `gh` joins the install hints. This overrides the PRD's non-goal \"no GitHub Releases mirroring\" for binaries: a binary release *is* a GitHub release.\n\n\nThe release record gains `assets`: the archives' names and sha256. The release's page lists them under Archives, from git, without asking GitHub.\n\n\nWith no `[release]` table, the Releases page shows what it found (`cmd/*/main.go`, a Makefile `dist` target, the remote and its forge, the default platforms), the TOML it will write, and **Enable binary release**. The server infers (`GET /api/releases/setup`), writes the table textually like `[github-project]` is written, keeping the file's comments (`POST /api/releases/setup`), and runs it at once. No field editing in the panel: edit `.git-board.toml` for anything else.\n\nLive checks go to guilbep/git-board-test only. git-board's own `.git-board.toml` gets the inferred block on this branch, so the next git-board release is cut from its Releases page."}},{"kind":"comment","author":"ee004d31386b76440a74651c79871f156633d4ff","time":1792575271,"origin":{"forge":"github.com/guilbep/git-board","event":"comment:6312766767"},"data":{"body":"Found while preparing the v0.9.0 cut, before clicking Cut:\n\n- **`build = \"make dist\"` fails in the cut's clean checkout.** The cut runs the build in a fresh `git worktree add --detach`, which has no `web/node_modules`. `make dist` depends on `web-build`, so it stops at `sh: quasar: command not found` (reproduced on a clean checkout of origin/main). The cut pushes the tag *before* `finish` → `binaries`, so this failure would leave v0.9.0 on origin with no GitHub release.\n- **Workaround on this repo:** `build = \"(cd web \u0026\u0026 npm ci) \u0026\u0026 make dist\"`. In a clean checkout it gives the 5 archives and `checksums.txt`, and the tree stays clean.\n- **To decide:** whether Enable binary release should infer that prerequisite (the Makefile's own comment says to run `npm ci` first), and what happens to a pushed tag whose build failed: does the next online cut or `reconcile` retry the build and publish, or does it need doing by hand?\n\nAlso: the Releases page was missing because `~/go/bin/git-board` had been built with `make install` from a stale `web/dist`. `install` doesn't depend on `web-build`.\n"}},{"kind":"comment","author":"ee004d31386b76440a74651c79871f156633d4ff","time":1792611697,"origin":{"forge":"github.com/guilbep/git-board","event":"comment:6324928681"},"data":{"body":"Done: git-board v0.9.0 was cut from its own Releases page (2026-10-21). Tag v0.9.0 is on f407a5c, and https://github.com/guilbep/git-board/releases/tag/v0.9.0 is Latest, with the 5 archives and `checksums.txt`. The darwin_arm64 archive verifies against `checksums.txt` and reports `v0.9.0`.\n\nOne gap remains: the inferred `build = \"make dist\"` needed `(cd web \u0026\u0026 npm ci) \u0026\u0026` in front before the cut could build in its clean checkout (see the comment above). That gap, and the failure-after-the-tag-is-pushed question, are filed as their own issue."}}]}